entry periodic-table
term: Periodic Table
related_terms: element
related_terms: atomic-number
related_terms: proton
related_terms: isotope
quick_facts: Elements are listed in order of atomic number
quick_facts: The big number in a box is the atomic number: the number of protons
quick_facts: The letters are a short symbol, such as C for carbon
quick_facts: Elements in the same column behave alike
quick_facts: Dmitri Mendeleev published an early version in 1869

sources:
    {"organization":"IUPAC","title":"Periodic Table of Elements","url":"https://iupac.org/what-we-do/periodic-table-of-elements/"}
    {"organization":"OpenStax","title":"Chemistry 2e: The Periodic Table","url":"https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/2-5-the-periodic-table"}

definition:
    A chart of all the known elements, in order of atomic number. Each box shows an element's atomic number, its symbol and its name. To use it, start with the number of protons and find that box: it names the element. Elements in the same column behave in similar ways, which is where the name comes from.
